      "text": "The orderly transition of power within the Texas Republican party was disrupted when a challenger, aided by an interventionist endorsement from the sitting president, secured a decisive 64% victory in the Senate runoff. This act of internal displacement rendered the incumbent, John Cornyn, the first sitting Republican senator from the state to lose renomination since 1970, fundamentally breaking the party's long-standing stability. The result establishes a new control structure, pitting the victor against a policy opponent in the upcoming general election.",
